my name is nari sol i'm a pianist  composer and recently i helped my mom  who is not a composer not a musician  write her very first piece of music i  did this because i find the act of  creating something original especially  music to be very therapeutic it can help  us get through some very dark and  difficult times  and recently  my mom's mother my grandmother  passed away and everybody was going  through a rough period i wanted to help  my mom process and express some of her  emotions by creating a piece of music in  memory of her mother and this is a  little bit about how we put all of this  together so the very first step was  actually to bring this idea up to my mom  and see if she would be up for the  challenge  so like i said she's not a musician and  this would be putting her way out of her  element and i also didn't want to burden  her with anything during this emotional  period but she said yes because she  loved the idea of doing something for my  grandmother and also i just assured her  that if she wants to stop at any time  she's free to do so the second step  involved just gathering as many memories  about my grandmother as we could in  order to help us brainstorm how we  instead of doing something somber she  wanted to write a piece of music that my  grandmother would have enjoyed and loved  it  so my grandma was a very joyful person  she really loved music she loved to sing  and dance she was always cracking jokes  and smiling and she made everybody  around her feel warm  um  [Music]  then i took my mom to the piano and my  first attempt at getting her started  kind of flopped  so i was just asking her if she can  think of a part of a melody or a  particular rhythm  if she liked a certain range in the  piano and all of this was way too vague  and i can tell my mom was losing a  little bit of confidence and she was  just lost  kromeon  so sure enough that evening my mom told  me that i should just write something on  my own that she didn't feel comfortable  composing but i wanted her to try one  more time because i felt that the way i  introduced this idea to her at the piano  was a bit flawed  the next day i took her outside with a  small keyboard already this is less  intimidating and i had some structure  i'll give you four pitches  [Music]  d  f  g  b flat  so i chose the pentatonic scale because  my grandmother was a huge fan of korean  trot music or trotsu and this sound is  present in most of the  so the major pentatonic scale has five  pitches  but i gave my mom four of those five  just to make it easier less intimidating  and  i made the first note that she would  naturally play  not the root because i find that if you  are overly focusing on the root note for  a melody it becomes a little square so  that's just a little adjustment i made  but i think it made a huge difference  [Music]  by giving her a solid framework and less  options to work with she seemed to come  up with ideas with more confidence and  ease  [Music]  wow  [Laughter]  foreign  once my mom finished her melody i  started to think of ways that i could  produce this for her  the key point here was to try to  incorporate as many things my  grandmother loved into the music the  music boxes  so this part of the process was very  meaningful for me because i was able to  sit down and remember so many little  details about my grandmother and  the way she appreciated music even  though we actually never talked about  music i knew that she appreciated the  sound of the piano many different  instruments  [Music]  in  [Music]  [Music]  while choosing the sounds and  instruments to put into the music  it was more about  remembering and imagining what she would  really enjoy rather than choosing things  that maybe sound better or i think sound  better  and this was very very special and it  gave me a chance to  feel close to her again with music  next i had my mom learn and practice her  music since i wanted her to actually  perform it herself i knew she could do  it even though we had a very limited  amount of preparation time and it was  also a great opportunity for her to go  back and review her music  she can change certain things she  actually changed her mind about the  rhythm in a few parts and about the  tempo  [Music]  you were  [Music]  and now we present to you pink pizzarang  or pink love  amma  oh  [Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  do  [Music]  [Music]  thank you for watching  if you haven't already please consider  subscribing to watch more videos about  the creative and technical sides of  making music and a very special thank  you to my patrons on patreon for making  these videos possible
 

